course: dictionary
lesson: 4649
title: What is history?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word history has more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one you need. «In school history lessons you learn about ancient Egypt, the Romans, and kings and queens.» Here history is a school subject, the lessons where you study the past.
explain: History can also mean everything that happened in the past. «History is the story of how people lived in the past.» This is the big meaning: all the things that happened over time.
explain: «The Kangxi Emperor ruled 61 years, 1661–1722, the longest reign in Chinese history.» Here history means the past of one country. Try your meaning in the sentence: the longest reign in Chinese past still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: History is everything that happened in the past, especially to people, countries and the world.
fact: History is also a school subject where you study the past.
fact: A timeline shows history in order: each step stands for the same number of years, like the marks on a ruler.
fact: «The Kangxi Emperor ruled 61 years, 1661–1722.» You can check this: 1722 minus 1661 is 61.
fact: To make history means to do something important that people will remember.
exercise: «In school history lessons you learn about ancient Egypt.» What is history in this sentence? | A kind of food | *The school subject where you study the past | A loud noise | A map of a city
exercise: «Her medical history includes two broken arms.» What does medical history mean? | Medicine you take today | A book about doctors | *Your past illnesses | Your next doctor visit
exercise: «The Kangxi Emperor ruled 61 years, 1661–1722, the longest reign in Chinese history.» How many years did he rule? | *61 | 1661 | 1722 | 100
test: Ella's team made history by winning the first cup ever. What does made history mean? | Lost the game badly | Wrote a book about football | *Did something important that people will remember | Forgot the past
test: Which one is a timeline? | A map of a city | A picture of a castle | *A line where each step stands for the same number of years | A list of your favourite foods
exam: Which one is a history, the meaning in «A history is a written account of past events»? | A map of the moon | A kind of school dinner | *A book that tells the story of past events | A game you play outside
